 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Liability Waiver Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a liability waiver form?\", \"a\": \"A liability waiver form is a document a participant signs before an activity to accept its risks and give up certain claims against the organizer. It is also called a liability release form. At its core it pairs a description of the hazards with a signed release.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a liability waiver form?\", \"a\": \"Start by writing down the activity and its hazards in plain sentences, then name who the release protects. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> turns that description into a simple liability waiver form with an initials box beside each risk and a signature at the end.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I get a waiver form?\", \"a\": \"Some government agencies post one at no cost. The California Department of Food and Agriculture, for one, publishes a Release and Waiver of Liability Agreement for fair events. Emergent is free to start, and a short description of your hazards is enough to build your own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a release of liability waiver form need to be notarized?\", \"a\": \"Not always. Many release forms rely on the signer's signature and the date alone. A notary can still add protection, because it makes the signature easier to prove if someone later disputes it. Your state's rules decide whether your activity calls for one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I use a sample liability waiver form as is?\", \"a\": \"Only as a starting draft. A sample liability waiver form was written for someone else's activity, so rewrite each hazard around what your participants do and keep one idea per clause. An attorney licensed in your state should read the final text before anyone signs.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who signs the waiver of liability form?\", \"a\": \"Each adult participant signs their own, because a family member cannot sign away another person's rights. A parent or legal guardian signs for a child. Some states may not enforce a parent's signature for a minor, which is worth raising with your attorney.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can participants sign an online waiver form before they arrive?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Put the link in the booking confirmation so most people sign at home, and keep a tablet at the desk for walk-ins. Because Emergent puts no cap on responses, a busy holiday weekend never closes the form. Pair it with a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/sign-in-form'>sign in form</a> if you also log who showed up.\"}, {\"q\": \"When do businesses use a liability release form?\", \"a\": \"Any time people do something physical under their care and an injury is a real possibility: rentals, guided trips, classes, volunteer days. For a one-day gathering with its own schedule and attendee list, an event waiver form fits better.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track when a liability release waiver form expires?\", \"a\": \"Give every signature an end date and keep it beside the signer's name. A season pass holder might renew each spring, while a drop-in visitor signs on every visit. With Emergent, that date lives on the signer's row in a database you own, and staff see a lapsed waiver before the person arrives.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which hazards should an activity waiver and release form include?\", \"a\": \"Each one a participant could face that day: equipment failure, sudden weather, mistakes by other participants, and the limits of their own fitness. Give every hazard its own clause and initials box. Keep photo consent off the waiver and collect it with a photo release form instead.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---how-to-step-7-des": "Vague language is a common reason waivers fail. Ask an attorney to review the text before the first real participant sees it. Then sign it yourself as a made-up participant, open the PDF and check every initials box came through."
 }
}